<title>CANADA: No frost seen in Canada's Prairies this week - EC.</title>
<headline>No frost seen in Canada's Prairies this week - EC.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>No frost was reported in Canada's Prairie grainbelt Tuesday morning and none was expected on the Prairies through Saturday, Environment Canada meteorologist Andre Pelland said.</p>
<p>A low pressure system moving out of Manitoba Tuesday should bring showers and a high of 20 to 23 degrees Celsius while a high pressure system over Saskatchewan and Alberta should lead to sunny skies and highs of 20 to 25 C, he said.</p>
<p>The Prairies were expected to remain dry throughout the week with temperatures warming up later in the week, he said.</p>
<p>Lows should range from eight to 10 degree C and highs were seen from 20 to 27 C through Friday.</p>
<p>Alberta should see showers Saturday morning, Pelland said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
